---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro"
import { statuses, simplifications } from "~/data/status"
---

<Base title="How we write these. Logic Benders">
  <main class="px-gutter flex max-w-225 flex-col gap-7 pt-12 pb-24">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(40px,6vw,80px)] leading-none font-extrabold tracking-tighter">
      How we write these
    </h1>
    <p>
      Every entry says what the paradox claims, in two sentences that both seem true. Then it
      says what gives. Where the answer is settled, we say so. Where it isn't, we say that
      instead and show the competing positions.
    </p>

    <h2 class="display mt-3 text-3xl">How a paradox ends</h2>
    <dl class="grid gap-3.5">
      {Object.values(statuses).map((s) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">{s.label}</dt>
          <dd class="m-0">{s.definition}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 class="display mt-3 text-3xl">How much we simplified</h2>
    <dl class="grid gap-3.5">
      {Object.values(simplifications).map((s) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">{s.label}</dt>
          <dd class="m-0">{s.definition}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 class="display mt-3 text-3xl">Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Each entry lists its sources. A verified entry has had its cited sources checked, and its
      claims brought into line with them. That does not mean every claim is undisputed: where
      experts disagree, the entry says so. An entry marked as unverified has not yet been
      checked and should not be relied on.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
